        "content": "| Module | Estimated Covered | Critical Gaps |\n|--------|-------------------|---------------|\n| `orchestrator.py` | ~0% | JSON preamble stripping, routing fallback, citation deduplication |\n| `base.py` | 0% | `build_prompt`, `NotImplementedError` from `process()` |\n| `engine.py` | ~10% | Cache hit/miss paths, stale fallback, `FetchError`, `_normalize_url` |\n| `cache.py` | 0% | TTL domain routing, `is_valid()`, `set_cached`, `health_check` |\n| `extractors.py` | ~20% | Truncation, fallback extraction, domain-specific selectors |\n| `db.py` | ~15% | Agent/orchestrator/feedback/cache CRUD, `clear_expired`, `list_queries` |\n| `routes.py` | 0% | All 5 endpoints including 404 and error paths |\n| `websocket.py` | 0% | `WebSocketManager` all methods, `process_query` error paths |\n\nThe most critical gaps are the **orchestrator JSON parsing**, the **fetch engine cache/error paths**, and the **WebSocketManager** — these are the hot paths that failures would surface in production. The `_normalize_url` rewrite in `engine.py` is a subtle correctness requirement that also has no test coverage.",
